From 4410972dc95dfbbbfd0c631018ca0d350079e021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:12:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Beginner clue scrolls

Beginner Treasure Trails: Read opens trail_cluetext (or the beginner map
interface) with the step, 21 steps (anagram and cryptic npc talks, emote steps
with Uri, map digs) in the server-only dbtable trail_beginner_steps, and the
reward casket rolled from the OSRS Wiki table (dbtable trail_beginner_casket)
into trail_rewardinv with the completion count message. Scroll box (beginner)
Open, and ::clue [step] [steps left].

NpcOpOverrides lets content take an npc op ahead of that npc's own handler for
the players it claims, so a clue step can take Talk-to on npcs that already
have dialogue (Cook, Hans, Doric, ...).
